#: colorscm.cpp:317
msgid ""
"<h1>Colors</h1> This module allows you to choose the color scheme used for "
"the KDE desktop. The different elements of the desktop, such as title bars, "
"menu text, etc., are called \"widgets\". You can choose the widget whose "
"color you want to change by selecting it from a list, or by clicking on a "
"graphic representation of the desktop.<p> You can save color settings as "
"complete color schemes, which can also be modified or deleted. KDE comes "
"with several predefined color schemes on which you can base your own.<p> All "
"KDE applications will obey the selected color scheme. Non-KDE applications "
"may also obey some or all of the color settings. See the \"Style\" control "
"module under \"Themes\" for more details."
msgstr ""

#: colorscm.cpp:379
msgid ""
"This color scheme could not be removed.\n"
"Perhaps you do not have permission to alter the file\n"
"system where the color scheme is stored."
msgstr ""
"Die kleurskema kon nie verwyder word nie.\n"
"Dalk het u nie regte om die lêerstelsel waar\n"
"die kleurskema gestoor is, te verander nie."

#: colorscm.cpp:429
msgid ""
"Please choose a unique name for the new color\n"
"scheme. The one you entered already appears\n"
"in the color scheme list."
msgstr ""
"Kies asb. 'n unieke naam vir die nuwe kleurskema.\n"
"die een wat u ingetik het bestaan alreeds in die\n"
"kleurskemalys."

